{"id": "1530614522572701747", "channel_id": "1530178712190845098", "author_id": "226712158845665281", "author_name": "zawaito", "content": "I feel we're getting tradeoffs for more tradeoffs. Like, what does Divine Chaos adds to the table?\n- double posse but you cant chose which posse to trigger (the tradeoff being you need keyflare equivalent to 2 posse since 2k in chaos already allows for double posse)\n- massive keyflare gain on the first card of each awakener but no keyflare on the subsequent ones (with the tradeoff being that to use any keyflare you need to get 2k of it)\n- 3 posses in a turn but both the posse and the order they trigger is completely random (while in normal chaos you can use one selected posse and then double dip on another random but selected posse)\n- chosen posse triggers on rouse but you can only rouse 4 times at most (the tradeoff being that you cant trigger your chosen posse anymore) (so now your chosen posse not only costs keyflare, but also either hand space if you want to prepare the rouse, or arithmetica if you want to use it right away)\n\nlike call me dramatic but everything this realm adds already comes with its own caveat/downside, yet we also got 3 substantial nerfs to chaos to \"balance it out\"", "timestamp": "2026-07-25T16:35:39.624000+00:00", "type": 19, "thread_id": "1530178712190845098", "mentions": ["718101727093456958"], "reply_to": "1530608574387191929"}
